#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Taskbar</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Taskbar</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The taskbar is a quick way to switch between applications. The taskbar can "
"be located in the panel (default), or outside the panel on the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "This module has options to control how the taskbar operates:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Show windows from all desktops</guilabel>, determines if all open "
"windows are included in the taskbar or not. By default, the taskbar only "
"shows the open windows <emphasis>on the current desktop</emphasis>. If this "
"option is enabled, the taskbar will show all open windows <emphasis>on all "
"desktops</emphasis>. <guilabel>Sort windows by desktop</guilabel> changes "
"the sort order of the icons on the taskbar, so that windows on virtual "
"desktop 1 are shown first (to the left, or at the top of the taskbar), "
"followed by windows on virtual desktop 2, and so on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Sort alphabetically by application name</guilabel> shows the icons "
"in an alphabetical sort order on the taskbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can have the taskbar <guilabel>Show only minimized windows</guilabel>. "
"In this case, when you minimize a window, it will show up on the taskbar, "
"and when you open it again, its taskbar entry will disappear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can disable <guilabel>Show application icons</guilabel>, and show just "
"the text. You might want to do this to save space on your taskbar, for "
"example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the <guilabel>Show window list button</guilabel> option, you can "
"enable a little button to be shown in the taskbar: this button will open a "
"popup menu offering access to applications on other desktops as well as some "
"useful actions, like <guilabel>Unclutter Windows</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Cascade Windows</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Group similar tasks</guilabel> allows you to save some space on "
"your taskbar, by only showing one icon for each running application, no "
"matter how many windows are shown. You can click on the icon to display a "
"menu of all the windows that are available. This is most useful when you "
"have enabled <guilabel>Show windows from all desktops</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next option allows you to set the <guilabel>Appearance</guilabel> to "
"<guilabel>Elegant</guilabel>, <guilabel>Classic</guilabel> or <guilabel>For "
"Transparency</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Actions"
msgstr "Accions"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next set of options allow you to customize the actions performed with "
"different mouse clicks on taskbar icons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select any action from the list for the <guilabel>Left button</"
"guilabel>, the <guilabel>Middle button</guilabel> and the <guilabel>Right "
"button</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "The options available are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Task List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Show the list of tasks grouped under the icon you have clicked on. If there "
"is only one task or window for that icon, it will become the active window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the default action for the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cycle Through Windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is more than one task grouped under the icon, switch from one to "
"the next, until you release the button (&ie; when you have reached the "
"window you are looking for). If there is only one task or window for that "
"icon, it will become the active window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the default action for the &MMB; if window grouping is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Operations Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Show the operations menu for the application. This allows you to minimize, "
"maximize, &etc;, move windows between desktops, and close windows. You can "
"perform these actions on all windows grouped under that icon, or on any "
"single window, by choosing it from the submenu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the default action for the &RMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Raise Task</guilabel>, <guilabel>Lower Task</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Minimize Task</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These three options make sense only if window grouping is disabled. They are "
"fairly self-explanatory. Raise means to make active, bring to the front, and "
"give focus. Lower means, send to the back, and give focus to whichever "
"window is now on top."
msgstr ""
